{"id": "en_story_dyatlov", "tag": "UNSOLVED", "cta": "MORE TRUE STORIES LIKE THIS", "ctaSmall": "follow", "ctaWhere": "new story every day", "accent": "#9BD3FF", "lang": "en", "total": 72.83, "segments": [{"text": "Between 1 and 2 February 1959, nine experienced hikers died on the slopes of Kholat Syakhl.", "start": 0.0, "end": 4.97}, {"text": "Their leader is Igor Dyatlov, but a tenth member named Yuri Yudin turned back days earlier.", "start": 5.8, "end": 10.24}, {"text": "He left the group early because of sudden illness and that decision saved his life.", "start": 10.74, "end": 14.0}, {"text": "High in the northern Urals, rescuers find a terrifying scene inside the frozen mountain camp.", "start": 14.74, "end": 19.34}, {"text": "The heavy hiking tent is mysteriously cut open from the inside by desperate human hands.", "start": 19.8, "end": 24.8}, {"text": "The frightened travelers fled directly into freezing temperatures of about minus 25 to 30 C.", "start": 24.8, "end": 29.383}, {"text": "Some victims ran away without proper winter boots, wearing only socks or going completely barefoot.", "start": 30.48, "end": 34.64}, {"text": "Rescuers eventually discover several bodies near the forest edge close to a small fire.", "start": 35.36, "end": 39.26}, {"text": "Over the decades, wild theories ranged from secret military weapons tests to visiting space aliens.", "start": 39.82, "end": 44.66}, {"text": "In 2020, Russian prosecutors finally named a sudden natural avalanche as the official cause.", "start": 45.28, "end": 49.9}, {"text": "Then in 2021, scientists Johan Gaume and Alexander Puzrin modeled a deadly slab avalanche.", "start": 50.6, "end": 56.12}, {"text": "They used special snow code originally created for the animation software in Disney film Frozen.", "start": 56.5, "end": 60.64}, {"text": "Even with modern science solving the snow mechanics, not every single haunting question is answered.", "start": 61.28, "end": 65.72}, {"text": "Will we ever truly know